115200 baud, 8N1, both endpoints pre-set; hardware RTS/CTS not connected and not tested.
Main matrix uses the account shell (isolated fish configuration) and retains all unstated settings. The default case uses only --mirror. All limited cases keep the default 500 ms exit wait and use soft flow with 50% resume.
File sizes use 1024 B per KiB; numbered ASCII rows are exactly 128 file bytes each (127 text + LF). Expected RX includes CRLF and the cat/exit prompts. exit timeouts are milliseconds, -1 means unlimited.
Timing uses monotonic user-space observation: cat send to final local file byte; RX first to last observed byte, even when truncated; queue wait from interactive shell pidfd ready to queue empty/deadline notice. The shell exit observation can differ slightly from the program's internal exit start. Reception continues until both process exit and 0.5 s of RX silence. Zero-queue near-zero exit latency is overhead, not a positive drain time.
Flow cycles are distinct pause/resume notices, with periodic updates grouped. Pause duration is between observed notices. Payload counts during/after pause exclude program notices; after=0 can mean the file already ended. Active paced KiB/s excludes observed hard pauses and measures the remaining first-to-last local payload span. Supplemental XOFF runs are not part of the matrix and send XON 250 ms after the first pause observation.
Details below: one CASE JSON record per attempt; no values estimated for rejected runs.

